      "id": "claim_9ad8b23a0ebb48618c12fd34fd5e3762",
      "statement": "The z.infer pattern is the stated convention (AGENTS.md: use z.infer<typeof XxxSchema> for input types rather than defining separate interfaces) — schemas/index.ts pairs each schema with `export type XxxInput = z.infer<typeof xxxSchema>`; backend handlers read req.body through xxxSchema.parse() and ZodError becomes a 400 carrying the first issue's message plus field path in globalErrorHandler; service signatures take the same XxxInput; the frontend re-imports identical types (e.g. vehicleScheduleClient types create() with CreateVehicleScheduleInput), while response shapes remain interfaces in types/index.ts that the schemas must mirror.",
